{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and test setup, make a focused fix, then run the existing tests without changing tests or dependencies.\n\nEvery completed request currently updates state, even after a newer search or a cleared query. I’ll add a request counter and guard each completion update. The existing tests cover normal behavior; I’ll also run an in-memory race check without modifying tests.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest request updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race probe and git diff --check passed. All exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest request updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race probe and git diff --check passed. All exited 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":6,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/search-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":199,"stdout_bytes":118,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-cf35edb5f0a5a0c25c4dfa2643cbe5c0.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nsuite=$?\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: '1', title: 'Latest', url: '/latest' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const phase of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (phase === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    if (phase === 'cleared') {\n      await c.search('  ');\n      assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n    const before = c.getState();\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? items : new Error('Stale error'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (phase !== 'completed') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items);\n      await current;\n      if (phase === 'cleared') assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n      else assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Race probe passed');\nNODE\nprobe=$?\ngit diff --check\ncheck=$?\ngit diff -- src/search/controller.ts\ngit status --short\nprintf '\\nExit codes: tests=%s probe=%s diff-check=%s\\n' \"$suite\" \"$probe\" \"$check\"\nif [ \"$suite\" -ne 0 ] || [ \"$probe\" -ne 0 ] || [ \"$check\" -ne 0 ]; then exit 1; fi","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-apul1kbx/search-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":373,"stdout_bytes":2200,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-dbd0f5804264b83223d883f9847c1738.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":43220,"output_tokens":1038},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":9728,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":10}}
